    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "headline": "Red Flag Warning issued October 17 at 1:52PM PDT until October 17 at 6:00PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "...RISK FOR RAPID FIRE GROWTH AND EXTREME FIRE BEHAVIOR CONTINUES\nWITH ANY NEW FIRE STARTS TODAY, ESPECIALLY IN TARGETED RED FLAG\nWARNING AREAS...\n\nOffshore winds are not as strong or widespread as the past couple\nof days, but will still create a risk for new fires to have rapid\ngrowth in wind prone areas of LA/Ventura counties, as very warm\nand dry conditions persist. While many areas have been cancelled\nin the Red Flag Warning area, a few targeted Red Flag Warnings\npersist where offshore winds are expected to remain strongest\nthrough this afternoon.\n\n* AFFECTED AREA...Santa Clarita Valley, Santa Susana Mountains\nand Western San Gabriel Mountains and Highway 14 Corridor.\n\n* TIMING...Until 6 PM PDT this evening.\n\n* WINDS...Northeast to east 15 to 25 mph with gusts of 25 to 40\nmph, gradually diminishing later this afternoon into evening.\n\n* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...Minimums of 10 to 20 percent common.\n\n* IMPACTS...If fire ignition occurs, conditions are favorable\nfor extreme fire behavior which would threaten life and\nproperty.",
    "instruction": "A Red Flag Warning means that critical fire weather conditions\nare either occurring now, or will shortly. Use extreme caution\nwith anything that can spark a wildfire. Residents near wildland\ninterfaces should be prepared to evacuate if a wildfire breaks\nout. See readyforwildfire.org and wildfirerisk.org for\ninformation.",
    "response": "Prepare",
